WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:19.920
I used to rule the world 
Seas would rise when I gave the word 

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.390
Now in the morning I sleep alone 
Sweep the streets I used to own

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:48.000
I used to roll the dice 
Feel the fear in my enemy’s eyes 

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:55.120
Listened as the crowd would sing 
Now the old king is dead long live the king 

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:02.000
One minute I held the key 
Next the walls were closed on me 

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:09.290
And I discovered that my castles stand 
Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:16.470
I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing 
Roman cavalry choirs are singing 

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:24.080
Be my mirror, my sword and shield 
Missionaries in a foreign field 

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:30.000
For some reason I can’t explain 
Once you’d gone there was never 

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:38.316
Never an honest word 
And that was when I ruled the world

00:01:50.488 --> 00:01:57.582
It was a wicked and wild wind 
Blew down the doors to let me in 

00:01:57.582 --> 00:02:04.414
Shattered windows and the sound of drums 
People couldn’t believe what I’d become 

00:02:04.414 --> 00:02:11.049
Revolutionaries wait 
For my head on a silver plate 

00:02:11.049 --> 00:02:19.520
Just a puppet on a lonely string 
Oh who would ever want to be king?

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:25.600
I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing 
Roman cavalry choirs are singing 

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:33.080
Be my mirror, my sword and shield 
My missionaries in a foreign field 

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:40.157
For some reason I can’t explain 
I know St Peter won’t call my name 

00:02:40.157 --> 00:02:46.676
Never an honest word 
But that was when I ruled the world

00:03:15.672 --> 00:03:22.294
Hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing 
Roman cavalry choirs are singing 

00:03:22.294 --> 00:03:29.376
Be my mirror, my sword and shield 
My missionaries in a foreign field 

00:03:29.376 --> 00:03:36.000
For some reason I can’t explain 
I know St Peter won’t call my name 

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:43.228
Never an honest word 
But that was when I ruled the world

